</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Clifford</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruni</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Mu&#x000f1;oz</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Bosch</surname><given-names>FX</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Worldwide prevalence and genotype distribution of cervical human papillomavirus DNA in women with normal cytology: a meta-analysis</article-title><source>Lancet Infect Dis</source><year>2007</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>453</fpage><lpage>459</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Lancet Infect Dis||7|453||bib3|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17597569</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib4"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Disease Control Priorities Project (DCPP)</collab></person-group><article-title/>AvailableAccessed: 02 October 2007</citation></ref><ref id="bib5"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Drummond</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Sculpher</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Torrance</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Brien</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Stoddart</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title/><source>Methods for the Economic Evaluation of Health Care Programs</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>New York, NY: Oxford University Press</publisher-name>(eds)3rd edn</citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duttagupta</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sengupta</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Roy</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sengupta</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhattacharya</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Laikangbam</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Roy</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghosh</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Das</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Are Muslim women less susceptible to oncogenic human papillomavirus infection? A study from rural eastern India</article-title><source>Int J Gynecol Cancer</source><year>2004</year><volume>14</volume><supplement>2</supplement><fpage>293</fpage><lpage>303</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Gynecol Cancer||14|293||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15086729</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ferlay</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bray</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Pisani</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Parkin</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>GLOBOCAN 2002: cancer incidence, mortality and prevalence worldwide, version 2.0. IARC Cancer Base No. 5</article-title><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Lyon, France: IARC Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Food and Drug Administration (FDA)</collab></person-group><article-title>FDA licenses new vaccine for prevention of cervical cancer and other diseases in females caused by human papillomavirus</article-title><year>2006</year>8 June 2006. Available atAccessed: 02 October 2007</citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Franceschi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rajkumar</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Snijders</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Arslan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahe</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Plummer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sankaranarayanan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Cherian</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Meijer</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiderpass</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Papillomavirus infection in rural women in southern India</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2005</year><volume>92</volume><supplement>3</supplement><fpage>601</fpage><lpage>606</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||92|601||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15668709</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Franceschi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rajkumar</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaccarella</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gajalakshmi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharmila</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Snijders</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Munoz</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Meijer</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Herrero</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human papillomavirus and risk factors for cervical cancer in Chennai, India: a case&#x02013;control study</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>2003</year><volume>107</volume><supplement>1</supplement><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>133</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Cancer||107|127||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12925967</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garnett</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>French</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldie</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modelling the impact of HPV vaccines on cervical cancer and screening programmes</article-title><source>Vaccine</source><year>2006</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>S178</fpage><lpage>S186</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Vaccine||24|S178||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16950005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gold</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Siegel</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>LB</given-names></name><name><surname>Weinstein</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cost-Effectiveness in Health and Medicine</article-title><year>1996</year><publisher-name>New York, NY: Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldhaber-Fiebert</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Stout</surname><given-names>NK</given-names></name><name><surname>Ortendahl</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuntz</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldie</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Salomon</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modeling human papillomavirus for analyses of screening and vaccination</article-title><source>Popul Health Metr</source><year>2007</year><volume>5</volume><supplement>1</supplement><fpage>11</fpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Popul Health Metr||5|11||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17967185</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldie</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaffikin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldhaber-Fiebert</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordillo-Tobar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahe</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wright</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><collab>Alliance for Cervical Cancer Prevention Cost Working Group</collab></person-group><article-title>Cost-effectiveness of cervical cancer screening in five developing countries</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>353</volume><supplement>20</supplement><fpage>2158</fpage><lpage>2168</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'N Engl J Med||353|2158||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16291985</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldie</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Grima</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kohli</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wright</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Weinstein</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Franco</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A comprehensive natural history model of HPV infection and cervical cancer to estimate the clinical impact of a prophylactic HPV-16/18 vaccine</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>2003</year><volume>106</volume><supplement>6</supplement><fpage>896</fpage><lpage>904</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Cancer||106|896||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12918067</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><cit